  "reason": "cl2 rule (owner 19:50, 10-15): ctlw RTL registers every leaf pin (issuer cfg/desc pin flops, raw rr capture rr_c, flop-driven rq/c_*/r_*/l_d_o/q*/bsel/lane_en/eg_* outputs); ot_pin_regs would add a second edge per port"
 },
 "floorplan_note": "HBM-B 10-17 ctlx: d4f binds ctlw with EGRESS_SPLIT 1, so xw_*/x_done/rwq/bq_d (5,121 of 10,920 pin bits) are open/undriven; ctlx drops them (5,799 pins). Faces follow the d4f neighbours: N rr/rq from the VM banks (vmb_<q>0..7 north of xl_<q>_ctl), E l_d_o to the two quantisers (xl_<q>_aqlo/aqhi east), W the x-store/BD/egress pair bundles, S the host F20 cfg/status + clocks. 388.8^2 (9 x 43.2): N 2,192 pins 5.6/um, E 2,055 5.3/um, W 1,224 3.1/um, S 337. Calendar SRAM SW corner beside its cfg pins and the clk_cal entry; clk entry S mid. | HBM-COLLQ/X 10-18 cl2p: +6 E pins (pv/po/pf) beside q*; same geometry.",
 "structural_change": "cl2p ctlx = main's ctlx (hgi_sm_xl2_ctlx, ot_hgi_sm_xload_cl2_ctlx, same 388.8^2 outline, faces, SRAM, clock entries) + x_fmt 3 (PRE-QUANTISED): 16-word exponent preload buffer, fmt 3 address stage, pv_lo/pv_hi bypass valids out and po/pf in on the E face beside qv/qo/qf; fmt 0/1/2 cycle-identical (bench +SAME=1). New master name; die swap xl_<q>_ctl -> cl2p_ctlx (xload_preq_binding.json).",
 "job": {
